═══ R8 EN reply complete (collagen/vegetarian) — guard: clean ═══
Q: I have spondylosis and osteoporosis and my doctor requires me to take collagen as part of treatment. But I have been a vegetarian for 14 years. Can I take normal collagen?
Sources: Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) | Buddhism Q&A (EN) | Metaphysics Q&A Vol 3 (EN) · types: qa_metaphysics,qa_general,introduction
  ✓ substantial reply (>600 chars)
  ✓ ends cleanly (punctuation/emoji, not mid-word)
  ✓ answers the vegetarian-collagen question
  ✓ final text passes guard (0 residual)
--- reply ---
Thank you for asking rather than just guessing 🙏 — 14 years of vegetarianism is a beautiful commitment, and it's clear you don't want to break it carelessly.

**First, on the collagen itself**

Master Lu addressed exactly this kind of situation in *Buddhism Q&A*:

> When you consume any medicine or health supplements that contain ingredients such as gelatine or fish oil, if your body does not reject the taste, then perhaps you have not reached the level where you are completely observing your precepts. However, it would still be best to avoid consuming such products as they contain animal by-products.

So the guidance is clear in order of preference:

1. **Look for a plant-based option first.** Speak to your doctor about vegan collagen boosters, or plant sources of what collagen supports — soy protein, calcium supplements, vitamin C, silica. Master Lu strongly recommends soy products, nuts, mushrooms, dairy and eggs (not quail/fertilised eggs) for vegetarians, precisely so the body stays strong.

2. **If your doctor says there is genuinely no substitute**, then take it as *medicine*, not as food. Before taking it, say in your heart:

   *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva forgive me, [your full name]. I am taking this only because I have no choice for my treatment. I absolutely do not wish to consume animal products."*

Master Lu emphasises that **intention is the deciding factor**. Taking medicine reluctantly for a bone condition is not the same as enjoying meat. The precept is broken when the mind enjoys it — not when the body is being treated.

**On the medical side**

Heart Dharma Door teaches body and mind together. Please keep following your doctor — spondylosis and osteoporosis need proper medical care. Chanting removes the spiritual obstruction; medicine treats the physical condition. Both hands, together.

**On the practice side**

You can pray specifically for these conditions:

📿 **Great Compassion Mantra** — 3 to 7 times daily
Before reciting: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless and heal me, [your full name], of my spine and bone condition, and restore my health."*

📿 **Heart Sutra** — 3 to 7 times daily
Before reciting: *"May the Greatly Merciful and Greatly Compassionate Guan Yin Bodhisattva bless me, [your full name], with wisdom and a clear, calm mind."*
(Not to be recited after 10pm)

May I ask — have you been reciting sutras before, or would this be new for you? That will help me suggest the right next step 🙏

Chanting resources: https://xinlingfamen.info/jingwen/

